  - given-names: Felipe
    family-names: Valencia de Almeida
    affiliation: "Escola Politécnica, Universidade de São Paulo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2031-6443"
  - given-names: Jorge
    family-names: Rady de Almeida
    name-suffix: Júnior
    affiliation: "Escola Politécnica, Universidade de São Paulo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3839-4570"
abstract: >-
  Run-level table of 600 OMNeT++ 5.7.1 / INET 4.2.10 simulation runs of the Routing Protocol
  for Low-Power and Lossy Networks (RPL): four static grids (36, 49, 64 and 100 nodes), five
  operating conditions (normal, flooding, blackhole, wormhole, manipulated medium-access backoff)
  and 30 seeded repetitions per cell. Each row is traceable to a published, unmodified scalar
  result file through its SHA-256. Supersedes the deprecated version 1.1, which must not be mixed
  with this version.
keywords:
  - RPL
  - wireless sensor networks
  - Industrial Internet of Things
  - OMNeT++
  - INET
  - blackhole
  - wormhole
  - flooding
  - backoff manipulation
  - intrusion detection
  - reproducibility
